    "chapter":  {
                    "number":  3,
                    "content":  [
                                    {
                                        "type":  "heading",
                                        "text":  "Jesus Heals on the Sabbath"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  1,
                                        "text":  "Once again Jesus entered the synagogue, and a man with a withered hand was there.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  2,
                                        "text":  "In order to accuse Jesus, they were watching to see if He would heal on the Sabbath.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  3,
                                        "text":  "Then Jesus said to the man with the withered hand, âStand up among us.â",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  4,
                                        "text":  "And He asked them, âWhich is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil, to save life or to destroy it?â\nBut they were silent.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  5,
                                        "text":  "Jesus looked around at them with anger and sorrow at their hardness of heart. Then He said to the man, âStretch out your hand.â So he stretched it out, and it was restored.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  6,
                                        "text":  "At this, the Pharisees went out and began plotting with the Herodians how they might kill Jesus.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "heading",
                                        "text":  "Jesus Heals the Multitudes"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  7,
                                        "text":  "So Jesus withdrew with His disciples to the sea, accompanied by a large crowd from Galilee, Judea,",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  8,
                                        "text":  "Jerusalem, Idumea, the region beyond the Jordan, and the vicinity of Tyre and Sidon. The large crowd came to Him when they heard what great things He was doing.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  9,
                                        "text":  "Jesus asked His disciples to have a boat ready for Him so that the crowd would not crush Him.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  10,
                                        "text":  "For He had healed so many that all who had diseases were pressing forward to touch Him.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  11,
                                        "text":  "And when the unclean spirits saw Him, they fell down before Him and cried out, âYou are the Son of God!â",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  12,
                                        "text":  "But He warned them sternly not to make Him known.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "heading",
                                        "text":  "The Twelve Apostles"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  13,
                                        "text":  "Then Jesus went up on the mountain and called for those He wanted, and they came to Him.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  14,
                                        "text":  "He appointed twelve of them, whom He designated as apostles, to accompany Him, to be sent out to preach,",
                                        "footnotes":  [
                                                          {
                                                              "noteId":  14,
                                                              "offset":  60,
                                                              "text":  "ECM, SBL, NE, BYZ, and TR do not include whom He designated as apostles.",
                                                              "caller":  "+"
                                                          }
                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  15,
                                        "text":  "and to have authority to drive out demons.",
                                        "footnotes":  [
                                                          {
                                                              "noteId":  15,
                                                              "offset":  21,
                                                              "text":  "BYZ and TR include to heal sicknesses, and",
                                                              "caller":  "+"
                                                          }
                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  16,
                                        "text":  "These are the twelve He appointed: Simon (whom He named Peter),",
                                        "footnotes":  [
                                                          {
                                                              "noteId":  16,
                                                              "offset":  34,
                                                              "text":  "SBL, NE, and WH; ECM, BYZ, and TR do not include These are the twelve He appointed.",
                                                              "caller":  "+"
                                                          }
                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  17,
                                        "text":  "James son of Zebedee and his brother John (whom He named Boanerges, meaning âSons of Thunderâ),",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  18,
                                        "text":  "Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, James son of Alphaeus, Thaddaeus, Simon the Zealot,",
                                        "footnotes":  [
                                                          {
                                                              "noteId":  17,
                                                              "offset":  97,
                                                              "text":  "Greek Simon the Cananean",
                                                              "caller":  "+"
                                                          }
                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  19,
                                        "text":  "and Judas Iscariot, who betrayed Jesus.",
                                        "footnotes":  [
                                                          {
                                                              "noteId":  18,
                                                              "offset":  39,
                                                              "text":  "Literally who also betrayed Him",
                                                              "caller":  "+"
                                                          }
                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "heading",
                                        "text":  "A House Divided"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  20,
                                        "text":  "Then Jesus went home, and once again a crowd gathered, so that He and His disciples could not even eat.",
                                        "footnotes":  [
                                                          {
                                                              "noteId":  19,
                                                              "offset":  21,
                                                              "text":  "Literally Then He comes to a house",
                                                              "caller":  "+"
                                                          }
                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  21,
                                        "text":  "When His family heard about this, they went out to take custody of Him, saying, âHe is out of His mind.â",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  22,
                                        "text":  "And the scribes who had come down from Jerusalem were saying, âHe is possessed by Beelzebul, â and, âBy the prince of the demons He drives out demons.â",
                                        "footnotes":  [
                                                          {
                                                              "noteId":  20,
                                                              "offset":  92,
                                                              "text":  "WH Beezeboul; Vulgate Beelzebub",
                                                              "caller":  "+"
                                                          }
                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  23,
                                        "text":  "So Jesus called them together and began to speak to them in parables: âHow can Satan drive out Satan?",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  24,
                                        "text":  "If a kingdom is divided against itself, it cannot stand.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  25,
                                        "text":  "If a house is divided against itself, it cannot stand.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  26,
                                        "text":  "And if Satan is divided and rises against himself, he cannot stand; his end has come.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  27,
                                        "text":  "Indeed, no one can enter a strong manâs house to steal his possessions unless he first ties up the strong man. Then he can plunder his house.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "heading",
                                        "text":  "The Unpardonable Sin"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  28,
                                        "text":  "Truly I tell you, the sons of men will be forgiven all sins and blasphemies, as many as they utter.",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  29,
                                        "text":  "But whoever blasphemes against the Holy Spirit will never be forgiven; he is guilty of eternal sin.â",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  30,
                                        "text":  "Jesus made this statement because they were saying, âHe has an unclean spirit.â",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "heading",
                                        "text":  "Jesusâ Mother and Brothers"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  31,
                                        "text":  "Then Jesusâ mother and brothers came and stood outside. They sent someone in to summon Him,",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  32,
                                        "text":  "and a crowd was sitting around Him. âLook,â He was told, âYour mother and brothers are outside, asking for You.â",
                                        "footnotes":  [
                                                          {
                                                              "noteId":  21,
                                                              "offset":  82,
                                                              "text":  "ECM, SBL, WH, and TR; NE and BYZ include and Your sisters.",
                                                              "caller":  "+"
                                                          }
                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "line_break"
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  33,
                                        "text":  "But Jesus replied, âWho are My mother and My brothers?â",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  34,
                                        "text":  "Looking at those seated in a circle around Him, He said, âHere are My mother and My brothers!",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "type":  "verse",
                                        "number":  35,
                                        "text":  "For whoever does the will of God is My brother and sister and mother.â",
                                        "footnotes":  [

                                                      ]
                                    }
                                ],
                    "footnotes":  [

                                  ]
                },
    "fullChapterApiLink":  "/api/BSB/MRK/3.json"
}
